        {
          "name": "@tangleai/store",
          "type": "patch"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "A contradiction is resolved as one operation: `MemoryStore` gains an optional atomic `mutate({ put, delete })` (the in-memory store has it), which `resolveContradictions` uses to write the superseded loser and its synthesized resolution together; on a store without it the resolution is written first and taken back if the loser cannot be written. A loser already superseded, by the same winner in a replayed pass or by another in a concurrent one, is counted as an application skip and never written again, so a replay no longer stores a second resolution.",
      "id": "atomic-contradiction"
    },
